Usage: shuf [OPTION]... [FILE]

Shuffle randomize lines.

Write a random permutation of the input lines to standard output.

Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.

Note: --random-seed uses a reproducible SHA3-256 + ChaCha12 path,
and --random-source follows the GNU/Microsoft-compatible entropy-
recycling adapter.

OPTIONS:
  -e, --echo               treat each ARG as an input line
  -i, --input-range ARG    treat each number LO through HI as an input line
  -n, --head-count ARG     output at most COUNT lines
  -o, --output ARG         write result to FILE instead of standard output
  -r, --repeat             output lines can be repeated
      --random-seed ARG    use STRING to initialize a reproducible random
                           permutation
      --random-source ARG  get random bytes from FILE
  -z, --zero-terminated    line delimiter is NUL, not newline
      --help               display this help and exit
  -V, --version            output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
